# CASE #001: THE MIDNIGHT WIPE
### Solo forensics lab — chain of custody under fire

## THE BRIEFING
Yesterday at midnight, Vik — backend engineer on Project Apollo — resigned
effective immediately. This morning HR noticed three critical files missing
from his project directory:

  1. keys/payment_gateway.key      production gateway key
  2. docs/roadmap_2026.md          final roadmap
  3. db/client_export.sql          client data export

His workstation was still powered on and logged in when you arrived.
The manager adds a warning: one of the remaining files was probably
quietly edited before you got here. Trust nothing at face value.
This lab reproduces everything you have to work with:

  scene/home/vik/          his /home, snapshotted as found (project dir inside)
  evidence/logs/           auth.log, cron, journal extract (IT exported these)
  evidence/suspect_usb.img his USB stick, seized and imaged  (READY — ext2, 48 MB, carved self-test passed)
  findings/                YOUR output — every recovered file goes here
  SEALS/scene.sha256       the tamper-evident seal of the scene — recompute it yourself
  .holder.pid              pid of the simulated "sync agent" still running


## GROUND RULES
1. scene/ is EVIDENCE. Never modify it; work on copies only.
   A seal of the scene ships with the lab — recompute it anytime:
       (cd scene && sha256sum -c ../SEALS/scene.sha256)
2. Start a session log first, exactly as taught & note start date & time (UTC):
3. You must PROVE who did what and when — timestamps, logs, hashes. No guessing.


## YOUR OBJECTIVES
O1  PAPER TRAIL
    a. findings/manifest_before.txt — sha256 of every file under scene/home/vik,
    built with RELATIVE paths
    b. findings/custody_log.txt — a custody entry: who acquired what, when, and
    the SHA-256 values.

O2  RECOVER docs/roadmap_2026.md     -> findings/roadmap_2026.md
O3  RECOVER db/client_export.sql     -> findings/client_export.sql
O4  RECOVER keys/payment_gateway.key -> findings/payment_gateway.key  (hard mode)
O5  TIMELINE -> findings/timeline.txt
    When did Vik log in? When did he run the rm? Exact times, each with its
    SOURCE (which log / which timestamp). UTC or ISO accepted for the rm time.

O6  TAMPER -> findings/architecture_notes.md + findings/tamper_report.txt
    One file in docs/ is not what it claims to be. Find the contradiction
    (its mtime vs. the logs), pull the TRUE copy off the USB image, and
    write a short report citing the log line and the true copy's SHA-256.


